### EDMS Webserver API
### For use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ's built-in HTTP client).
### Generated from routes in src/main.rs (67 routes, verified against main.rs on 2026-09-15).
###
### Some routes below are WebSocket-only and cannot be driven from this file — they are
### marked "WS ONLY" and left commented out. Use a WS client (e.g. websocat, browser
### devtools) against ws://localhost:3000/<path> instead.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

# ============================================================
# Views
# ============================================================

### Home view metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/home

### Test view metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/test-view

### List view metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/list-view

# ============================================================
# Endpoints CRUD
# ============================================================

### Create an endpoint
# "method" is optional — GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE only, 400 if invalid.
# Omitting it leaves the endpoint unclassified in the CRUD Operations table.
# Side effect: triggers a dashboard snapshot refresh (dashboard.db) on success.
POST {{baseUrl}}/endpoints/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint_id": "get-user-profile",
  "endpoint_str": "https://api.example.com/users/{id}",
  "annotation": "Fetches a user profile by id",
  "method": "GET"
}

### Delete an endpoint
# Side effect: same dashboard snapshot refresh as create, on success.
POST {{baseUrl}}/endpoints/get-user-profile/delete

### Set/replace an endpoint's annotation after creation
# 404 if the endpoint doesn't exist. Side effects: dashboard snapshot
# refresh + broadcasts EndpointAnnotationUpdated on the shared WS channel.
POST {{baseUrl}}/endpoints/get-user-profile/annotation
Content-Type: application/json

{ "annotation": "Updated: now paginated" }

### Look up an endpoint by exact (endpoint_str, method) — dedup check
# before running a test, so a re-tested URL reuses its endpoint_id
# instead of a new one getting allocated. 404 if none exists.
GET {{baseUrl}}/endpoints/lookup?endpoint_str=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.example.com%2Fusers%2F%7Bid%7D&method=GET

# ============================================================
# Test View
# ============================================================

### Get a saved request for one test run (the "QP" for that run)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test-view/get-user-profile/request/1

### Get the saved response for one test run
GET {{baseUrl}}/test-view/get-user-profile/response/1

### Get the saved request/response headers for one test run
# Body shape: {"request_headers": {...}, "response_headers": {...}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/test-view/get-user-profile/headers/1

### List every QP pair (test run) saved for an endpoint, oldest first
# Each entry: {request_number, method, timestamp, status_code, response_time_ms}.
# status_code/response_time_ms are null if the response hasn't landed yet.
GET {{baseUrl}}/test-view/get-user-profile/qps

### Delete one QP pair
# Removes its request_metadata/response_metadata rows and the three saved
# JSON files (request/response/headers). 404 if no such pair exists.
# Side effect: broadcasts QpDeleted on the shared WS channel (same one
# /test-view/run uses) so open List/Test Views know to re-fetch the list above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-view/get-user-profile/qps/1/delete

### Stop the current test run
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-view/stop

### Save a test run to history
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-view/save/history
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint_id": "get-user-profile",
  "action": "test",
  "details": "manual run from api.http"
}

### Save a bookmark
# "collection" is required as of 2026-09-22 — no more implicit "loaded"
# collection to fall back to. Side effect: dashboard snapshot refresh.
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-view/save/bookmark
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "collection": "auth-suite",
  "endpoint_id": "get-user-profile",
  "notes": "known-good response, keep for regression checks"
}

### Clear all history
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-view/history/clearall

### Clear one collection's bookmarks (not every collection's)
# Side effect: triggers a dashboard snapshot refresh.
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-view/auth-suite/bookmark/clearall

### WS ONLY — subscribe to live endpoint list: GET /test-view/endpoints/load
### WS ONLY — subscribe to one collection's live bookmark list:
### GET /test-view/{collection}/bookmarks/load
### Each entry includes "updated" (when it was bookmarked) and
### "in_collection" (has it also been saved as a real member, vs. just
### bookmarked). Multiple tabs on the same collection all see the same
### live updates; different collections never interfere (2026-09-22).
### WS ONLY — run a test (send {"type":"...","payload":{"endpoint_id","method","body","timeout_ms","tick_interval_ms"}}): GET /test-view/run
### WS ONLY — bookmark into a named collection (also triggers a dashboard
### snapshot refresh): GET /test-view/{collection}/add
### WS ONLY — remove a bookmark entirely, not just membership (also
### triggers a dashboard snapshot refresh): GET /test-view/{collection}/delete

# ============================================================
# Tags
# ============================================================
# add/remove (not list or popular) trigger a live dashboard snapshot refresh,
# same as endpoint create/delete.

### Add a tag to an endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags/get-user-profile/add
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tag": "critical" }

### Remove a tag from an endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags/get-user-profile/remove
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tag": "critical" }

### List tags for an endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/get-user-profile

### Most-used tags across all endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/popular

# ============================================================
# Bookmarks ↔ Collections — multiple collections at once (2026-09-22)
# ============================================================
# Redesigned so a collection is always explicit in the request instead of
# an implicit shared "active" one — two tabs can now have two different
# collections open with no interference, and two tabs on the same
# collection both see the same live updates. See API_REFERENCE.md for
# the full rationale and the cascades that come with it (collection
# rename/delete, endpoint delete all correctly clean up bookmarks now).

### WS ONLY — snapshot of a collection's bookmark count, then streams
### events. Pure read — no wipe, no copy, no backup: GET /bookmarks/{collection}/load

### Save a bookmarked endpoint into real collection membership
# 400 if it isn't currently bookmarked in this collection. Broadcasts
# CollectionMembershipUpdated — previously this emitted nothing at all.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookmarks/auth-suite/get-user-profile/save

### Remove an endpoint's membership from a collection — stays bookmarked
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookmarks/auth-suite/get-user-profile/unsave

# ============================================================
# Collections / Webview / Repoview
# ============================================================
# Catalog (which collections/webviews/repoviews exist) + a per-view
# tagname+count table — a simple incrementally-maintained counter, not a
# full tag entity with membership tracking. Per Ravi's schema, 2026-08-25.
#
# create/delete/rename on the tags routes all trigger a dashboard snapshot
# refresh AND broadcast a ViewTagsUpdated event on the app's single shared
# WS channel (same channel /test-view/run uses) — connect there to know
# when to re-fetch the matching */tags/list route below, per the WS-vs-REST
# rule: WS only triggers a refresh, REST delivers the actual data.
#
# WS event shape:
#   {"type":"event","event":{"type":"ViewTagsUpdated","payload":{"view":"collections"}}}
#   "view" is one of "collections" | "webview" | "repoview".
#
# Not built yet: bookmarks/eqptags (same pattern is planned for it), the
# "merge" operation, and the per-collection independent SQLite file
# (file_path on the catalog entry stays null until that exists).

### Register a new collection in the catalog
# "annotation" is optional.
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "auth-suite", "annotation": "Auth regression suite" }

### List registered collections
# Each entry includes "annotation" (null if unset) and "endpoint_count"
# (null if the collection has no file yet).
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/list

### Get one collection's catalog entry
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite

### Set/replace a collection's annotation
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/annotation
Content-Type: application/json

{ "annotation": "Auth regression suite — updated" }

### Rename a collection — moves its file on disk to match, too
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "new_name": "auth-suite-v2" }

### Delete a collection's catalog entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite-v2/delete

### List endpoints that belong to a collection
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/endpoints

### Add to Collection — find every endpoint carrying any of these tags,
# add them as members, and optionally copy their current tags in too.
# Central tags table is read-only here, never modified.
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/tags/import
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tags": ["smoke", "critical"], "export_existing_tags": true }

### List (endpoint_id, tag) pairs this collection carries from the import above
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/tags/endpoints

### Remove an endpoint from a collection
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/endpoints/remove
Content-Type: application/json

{ "endpoint_id": "get-user-profile" }

### Add a membership tag to a collection (distinct from the catalog-wide
### collections/tags/* counters above — these are per-collection C(T) rows)
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/membership-tags/add
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tag": "smoke" }

### Remove a membership tag from a collection
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/membership-tags/remove
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tag": "smoke" }

### List a collection's membership tags
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/auth-suite/membership-tags

### List all collections that carry a given membership tag
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/by-tag/smoke

### Create a collections tag, or add to its count if it already exists
# "endpoint_ids" length becomes the count increment (defaults to 1 if omitted/empty).
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/tags/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "auth", "endpoint_ids": ["E1", "E2"] }

### Delete one or more collections tags in one call
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/tags/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": ["auth"] }

### Rename a collections tag — its count carries over to the new name
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/tags/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "old_name": "auth", "new_name": "authn" }

### List collections tags with their counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/tags/list

### --- Same four "tags" routes + catalog create/list, scoped to webview ---

POST {{baseUrl}}/webview/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "wtest" }

### List registered webviews
GET {{baseUrl}}/webview/list

### Create a webview tag, or add to its count if it already exists
POST {{baseUrl}}/webview/tags/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "auth", "endpoint_ids": ["E1"] }

### Delete one or more webview tags in one call
POST {{baseUrl}}/webview/tags/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": ["auth"] }

### Rename a webview tag
POST {{baseUrl}}/webview/tags/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "old_name": "auth", "new_name": "authn" }

### List webview tags with their counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/webview/tags/list

### --- Repoview: a real per-instance directory, copied FROM a collection ---
# Unlike webview/collections tags below, repoview also has its own
# membership + real copied data — see API_REFERENCE.md's Repoview section.

### Create a repoview from a collection — copies real request/response/
# header files for the given endpoint_ids (or every member, if omitted).
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "rtest", "annotation": "optional", "source_collection": "product-catalog" }

### Bulk delete — each name deleted independently, one bad name doesn't
# block the rest. Always 200; check each entry's own "ok" in results.
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": ["rtest", "rtest-2"] }

### List registered repoviews (catalog rows only, no aggregate stats)
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/list

### One repoview's full stats: eid_count, data_size_bytes, qp_count,
# tags_in_data, crud_types, source
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest

### List a repoview's member endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest/endpoints

### List the per-endpoint tags this repoview carries in its own copy —
# auto-copied at create time, separate from tags_in_data (read live from
# the central table) and from membership-tags (tags on the row itself).
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest/tags/endpoints

### Remove one member — also deletes its copied data from this repoview
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest/endpoints/remove
Content-Type: application/json

{ "endpoint_id": "E0001-AAA" }

### Rename a repoview — moves the whole directory, not just one file
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "new_name": "rtest-renamed" }

### Annotate a repoview
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/annotation
Content-Type: application/json

{ "annotation": "updated" }

### Duplicate a repoview — clones the whole directory, annotation, source,
# and row-level tags under a new name. No regeneration of Tables-*.md;
# the underlying data doesn't change on duplicate, so the copy is correct
# as-is.
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/duplicate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "new_name": "rtest-renamed-copy" }

### Delete a repoview — removes the catalog row and the whole directory
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/delete

### --- Row-level tags on the RepoView instance itself (modifiable "Tags" ---
### field from the spec) — separate from tags_in_data (aggregate, from the
### copied endpoint data) and from the central rollup below.

### Add a tag to a repoview
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/membership-tags/add
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tag": "production" }

### Remove a tag from a repoview
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/membership-tags/remove
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tag": "production" }

### List a repoview's own tags
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/membership-tags

### Find every repoview carrying a given tag
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/by-tag/production

### --- Index Table generation ---
# Two approaches, one active at a time (both write the same Tables-NNN.md /
# Tables-meta.md names, so generating one replaces the other). Replaces every
# existing Tables-*.md on each call. Not run automatically on create or on
# membership changes - call this whenever you want the files refreshed.
# NOTE: a JSON body is always required, even if just {}.

### Approach [B] Endpoint Segments (the default) with the default batch size (100)
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tables/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Approach [B] with an explicit batch size
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tables/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approach": "endpoint_segments", "batch_size": 50 }

### Approach [A] Sorted Tags - tag -> segment-count pivot, untagged last
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tables/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approach": "sorted_tags", "batch_size": 50 }

### --- Reading the generated files back (what the UI's "Endpoint Data table"
### click loads) ---

### Which files exist right now, and which approach produced them
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tables

### The markdown of the master/navigation file, then of one batch
# Only Tables-meta.md and Tables-<number>.md are ever served.
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tables/Tables-meta.md

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tables/Tables-001.md

### --- Two-way merge: Collections <> RepoView ---

### Collection -> RepoView, after creation: merge members of ANY collection
# in (omit endpoint_ids for all of them). Existing members are refreshed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/endpoints/add
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source_collection": "content-api", "endpoint_ids": ["E0001-AAA"] }

### Via Tag Ops: merge in every endpoint carrying any of these central tags
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/tags/import
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tags": ["production"] }

### RepoView -> Collection. Endpoints that no longer exist centrally are
# rebuilt from the RepoView's own copy under their ORIGINAL ids; anything
# that still exists centrally is left untouched. Skipped members (no
# snapshot / URL+method now owned by another endpoint) are reported in
# results and not added; top-level ok is false if any were skipped.
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/rtest-renamed/export-to-collection
Content-Type: application/json

{ "collection": "recovered", "create_if_missing": true }

### --- Same four "tags" routes as webview above, scoped to repoview ---
# (central tag-count rollup, separate from the membership routes above)

### Create a repoview tag, or add to its count if it already exists
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/tags/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "auth", "endpoint_ids": ["E1"] }

### Delete one or more repoview tags in one call
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/tags/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": ["auth"] }

### Rename a repoview tag
POST {{baseUrl}}/repoview/tags/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "old_name": "auth", "new_name": "authn" }

### List repoview tags with their counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/repoview/tags/list

# ============================================================
# Data View
# ============================================================

### Delete a data folder
POST {{baseUrl}}/dataview/my-folder/delete

### Merge a data folder (fire-and-forget — returns 202 immediately,
### result arrives later via POST /internal/callback -> ExportReady event)
POST {{baseUrl}}/dataview/my-folder/merge

### WS ONLY — mark a folder active (syncs to disk, broadcasts FolderBecameActive): GET /dataview/{folder}/active

### Live active-folder dashboard counts (endpoints / bookmarks / history)
# NOTE: this is NOT the dashboard_snapshots table from dashboard_db.rs —
# it's a separate, older live-count endpoint scoped to the active folder.
# See the "Dashboard Snapshot" section below for the snapshot data.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dataview/dashboard

# ============================================================
# Dashboard Snapshot
# ============================================================

### Latest dashboard snapshot (endpoint/bookmark/tag counts, DB size,
### storage size, file count) — taken on startup, and refreshed live after
### any endpoint create/delete, tag add/remove, or bookmark/collection
### action (see side-effect notes on those routes above).
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/snapshot

### Full snapshot history, oldest first (rolling 30-day retention window)
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/snapshot/history

### Static data — hardcoded config loaded from config.yaml at startup:
### application limits, stability/commit info, external links.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/static

### Day-over-day comparison between two arbitrary dates (not necessarily
### adjacent — e.g. day 1 vs day 6). Dates are "YYYY-MM-DD". 404 if either
### date has no daily snapshot — response distinguishes "outside the 30-day
### retention window" from "no data yet" (today/future/app was down that day).
### Daily snapshots are captured automatically once per calendar-date
### rollover (a background watcher, not a request you trigger).
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/compare?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-07

### CRUD Operations breakdown (endpoint segments/tags/bookmarks/history/QP
### pairs, grouped by HTTP method with count + % of that row's total).
### Ravi's [1] approach: global processing via a compute child process,
### triggered by app launch + this refresh route — never per-transaction.
### 404 until the first refresh (startup or manual) completes.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/crud-operations

### Trigger a CRUD Operations recompute — this is what the dashboard's
### Refresh button hits. Fire-and-forget: 202 immediately, result lands a
### moment later via POST /internal/callback.
POST {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/crud-operations/refresh

# ============================================================
# Logs
# ============================================================

### Plain-text tail of the app log (last 500 lines, oldest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/logs

# ============================================================
# Repo Export
# ============================================================

### Export a bookmark collection
# Returns markdown immediately; also fires async zip export + markdown
# generation jobs in the background (results via /internal/callback).
GET {{baseUrl}}/repo/my-collection/export.zip/export

### Import a previously exported zip back into a collection
# Fire-and-forget: 202 immediately, looks for the zip under
# edms_root/exports/{filename}, result via /internal/callback.
POST {{baseUrl}}/repo/my-collection/export.zip/import

# ============================================================
# Internal (do not call from the UI — edms-child callback channel only)
# ============================================================

# POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/callback
